Track 1: Iron Oxide Chews the Sprocket
- Story & Context: At the Soda Lake trading camp, an afternoon squall overturned an open trailer carrying three waterlogged Akai samplers, scattering their circuit boards across the wet salt crust. Boyd Kaelen salvaged two fried boards with a butane iron, patching them directly into a sun-warped polyphonic synth and hitting record just as an argument over stolen generator kerosene escalated into a knife brawl beside the stage. Mara Vance clamped her fiddle under her jaw and sawed furiously against Boyd's runaway 172 BPM breakbeat to drown out the shouting, howling, "Let the dry tooth take the wire!" The track preserves the raw tape flutter and microphone feedback from that evening, freezing the riot that gave the subculture its inaugural anthem.
